cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RACING, please cite this software (and, where relevant, the underlying ACIER study referenced in the README)."
title: "RACING: R-based Attractor Complexity INdex for Gait"
abstract: "Open R implementation of validated linear and nonlinear gait-analysis algorithms for triaxial lower-back accelerometer data, ported from the ACIER MATLAB code. Computes local dynamic stability (LDS), the attractor complexity index (ACI), step/stride regularity, step frequency, and RMS measures, following FAIR principles."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Terrier
    given-names: Philippe
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3693-4505"
    affiliation: "HE-Arc Sante, HES-SO University of Applied Sciences and Arts Western Switzerland, Neuchatel, Switzerland"
version: "1.0.2"
date-released: "2026-06-04"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ph-Terrier/RACING-gait-analysis"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.18801995"
keywords:
  - gait analysis
  - accelerometry
  - nonlinear dynamics
  - local dynamic stability
  - attractor complexity index
  - gait variability
  - fall risk
  - R
  - FAIR
  - biomechanics
